{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "MosaicMtemBinaryLogGamma",
    "description": "The binary activity coefficients of MOSAIC's Multicomponent Taylor Expansion Method (MTEM; Zaveri, Easter and Wexler 2005): SUBROUTINE mtem_compute_log_gamz with FUNCTION fnlog_gamz of chem/module_mosaic_therm.F (WRF v4.8.0, :9554-9787 and :16399-16418).\n\nMTEM writes the activity coefficient of electrolyte A in a mixed solution as a mole-fraction-weighted mean of log10 gamma_A in BINARY solutions of each electrolyte E at the same water activity (mtem_activities.esm applies that mixing rule). This component supplies the binary values: log10 gamma_{A(E)} = sum_{p=1..6} b_mtem[p, A, E] a^{p-1}, a polynomial in the water activity, held at or above the fit's lower limit, a = max(a_w, a_min,E). Unlike the binary molality (aerosol_water_zsr.esm) there is no upper cap.\n\nWHICH WATER ACTIVITY. The Fortran evaluates these once per grid cell, in update_thermodynamic_constants, at the AMBIENT relative humidity ah2o -- not at the per-bin, Kelvin-adjusted ah2o_a(ibin) that the ZSR water uses. A consumer must pass the cell's relative humidity here even where the bins' water activities differ.\n\nWHICH PAIRS. mtem_compute_log_gamz assigns only the pairs its A-by-E listing names (15 partners for HNO3, HCl, (NH4)2SO4 and the other sulfate-rich-capable electrolytes, 10 for the sulfate-poor-only salts); every other entry of log_gamz keeps its initial zero. b_mtem is zero outside the listed pairs too, so the polynomial reproduces the zeros without a mask; the tests pin the full matrix, listed pairs and zeros alike.\n\nPRECISION. b_mtem and aw_min are binary32 roundings widened to double (mosaic_thermo_parameters.esm); the polynomial is evaluated in double. The Fortran uses Horner's form, this component the power sum it equals.\n\nTESTS AND COVERAGE. Four levels (relative humidity 0.30 to 0.61), all 484 entries each, against the in-model log_gamz at rel 1e-9 (non-zero entries; measured 1.3e-10 worst over 944 level-steps, the polynomial cancelling near its zeros) and exactly where the Fortran leaves zero. NOT exercised: the a_min floor, since the relative humidity stays above the 0.1 of every listed solvent and the three solvents with a_min = 1 (H.HSO4, CaSO4, CaCO3) carry no listed pair -- removing the floor changes no assertion.",
    "authors": [
      "EqWeFiC"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Zaveri, R.A., Easter, R.C., Wexler, A.S. (2005). A new method for multicomponent activity coefficients of electrolytes in aqueous atmospheric aerosols. J. Geophys. Res. 110, D02201."
      },
      {
        "citation": "WRF v4.8.0 chem/module_mosaic_therm.F"
      }
    ]
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "NEL": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 22,
      "description": "Number of MOSAIC electrolytes (nelectrolyte)."
    }
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "el": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": "NEL"
    },
    "solv": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": "NEL"
    },
    "pc": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 6
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "MosaicMtemBinaryLogGamma": {
      "subsystems": {
        "tp": {
          "ref": "./mosaic_thermo_parameters.esm"
        }
      },
      "variables": {
        "a_w": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.8,
          "description": "The grid cell's ambient relative humidity as a fraction (ah2o), NOT the per-bin Kelvin-adjusted water activity."
        },
        "a_fit": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "solv"
          ],
          "description": "Water activity held at or above each solvent electrolyte's fit limit, max(a_w, a_min,E)."
        },
        "log_gamz": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "1",
          "shape": [
            "el",
            "solv"
          ],
          "description": "log10 of the binary activity coefficient of electrolyte A (first index) in a binary solution of electrolyte E (second index) at water activity a_w. The solvent axis has its own index set, solv (same size), so a consumer and an assertion can name the two axes apart."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": "a_fit",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "faq",
            "output_idx": [
              "e"
            ],
            "args": [],
            "ranges": {
              "e": {
                "from": "solv"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "max",
              "args": [
                "a_w",
                {
                  "op": "index",
                  "args": [
                    "tp.aw_min",
                    "e"
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "log_gamz",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "faq",
            "output_idx": [
              "a",
              "e"
            ],
            "args": [],
            "ranges": {
              "a": {
                "from": "el"
              },
              "e": {
                "from": "solv"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "faq",
              "output_idx": [],
              "reduce": "+",
              "args": [],
              "ranges": {
                "p": {
                  "from": "pc"
                }
              },
              "expr": {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "index",
                    "args": [
                      "tp.b_mtem",
                      "p",
                      "a",
                      "e"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "^",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "index",
                        "args": [
                          "a_fit",
                          "e"
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "op": "-",
                        "args": [
                          "p",
                          1
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "mtem_s918_lev1",
          "description": "Surface layer, mid-afternoon (relative humidity 0.50): model step 918, level 1; relative humidity 0.495738 (relhumclm, the value update_thermodynamic_constants evaluates log_gamz at -- not the rh_pc*0.01 that aerosol_phase_state later stores in ah2o, N118). Reference: the em_scm_xy chem_opt = 170 column (data/eqwefic/chem170_scm, reference namelist unchanged), MOSAIC thermodynamics capture dumps/chem170_mosaic_therm (WRF fork earthsciml-instrumented-chem170, the compute_activities hooks), whose fields shared with dumps/chem170_mosaic_coag are bit-identical. The thermodynamics runs in real(kind=8), so the in-model values are a double-precision reference; all 484 entries, the 166 pairs mtem_compute_log_gamz lists at rel 1e-09 (measured 1.3e-10 worst over 944 level-steps: the polynomial cancels near its zeros) and the 318 it leaves at zero exactly.",
          "parameter_overrides": {
            "a_w": 0.4957381784915924
          },
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 1
          },
